# Runtime operator flags raised by the loop for a HUMAN, per product.
#
# The root .gitignore already lists HOTFIX_NEEDED.md / SPEED_STORY_NEEDED.md,
# but it is frozen byte-unchanged from HEAD by 26 permanent every-suite guards
# (`git diff --quiet HEAD -- dispatcher.py scripts/ .gitignore`, tests iter
# 50-84), so a new entry there reddens the suite of the very iteration that adds
# it. A nested .gitignore is the same semantics on an unfrozen path: git honors
# it for everything under products/.
#
# The iter-141 liveness flag: raised when shipped iterations are inert in the
# running brain, auto-cleared once it is restarted. Per-run state, never source.
*/RESTART_NEEDED.md

# The 5th team's wiring, written by the OPERATOR outside the loop. It was untracked AND unignored,
# which armed BOTH of the loop's git bulk verbs against it:
#   * the ship gate's `git add -A` would commit a foreign team's config into an unrelated release
#     diff (a release commit must contain only this iteration's work);
#   * the revert path's `git clean -fd` DELETED it -- twice: iteration 173's gate caught it and
#     restored it from the operator's backup, and it was missing again when 174 opened.
# One entry closes both, because `git clean -fd` WITHOUT `-x` spares ignored paths, and an ignored
# path is never staged by `add -A`. Named as exactly ONE literal path, deliberately NOT a wildcard
# over every team's config file: products/_platform/config.json and products/repolens/config.json
# are TRACKED SOURCE, and a wildcard would advertise them as runtime state to every future reader.
# `dispatcher.py` swallows a config load failure BY DESIGN and reads the roster at STARTUP ONLY, so
# losing this file has no loud symptom -- team 5 just silently never takes a shift.
agent-gap-radar/config.json
